<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a51b88268bef8f82706ee52f5011fd825e183ea06faf5fce7c6b7ce075530ac</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432--cd7bb6e11389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Felix Nmecha's "Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8539a046af592025f58dea02da59c24afb210201ec578751465f5f0e69de1225</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88f8269025894ca782f1efc82a72a937875f0cfba57f5559eaecfba60986e913</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Will Jürgen Klopp's charisma be enough for Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bb3686f63e592c62d0323e1b25defbb9831c7205407fbe7817e0955d1e85fb2</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-j_rgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266--fed309f9f1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-jürgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After defeat to Greece, Jürgen Klopp faces the first real test of his tenure as coach of Germany's national men's football team. Can his charisma alone push this group forward?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's ice hockey team says Russia replacing it at World Juniors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:084452d2d2ec1ba44ec4d0ab013658b5dfa21ace8375390e03f13dcebbab99ee</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844--43300d3ba1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07063d4a79eaf56095e5e63d2f274c9920a6966789e20ff42776158669a6324e</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the IIHF Women's Ice Hockey World Championship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38af1a43d739d9a947c8f726150b400ed91f4471b98b2c7c4e1517fa306aca6d</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148--d773b0d8af6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As ice hockey's governing body continues to wrangle over how to respond to a CAS order to reinstate Russia to international play, the top women's tournament gets underway in Denmark without Russia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
